              "content": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "The rate law for an elementary step is based directly on its molecularity (stoichiometry). The rate law for an overall reaction is determined by experiment (not from the stoichiometry)."
                    }
                  ],
                  "id": "xmzrnvq5quj3pr5",
                  "type": "p"
                }
              ],
              "id": "3649169931"
            },
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "Compare the known rate law for the overall reaction with the rate law that would result if the reaction occurred as an elementary step."
                    }
                  ],
                  "id": "uj7dszce8ej09k0",
                  "type": "p"
                }
              ],
              "id": "1675413460"
            },
            {
              "content": [
                {
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "If the known rate law for the overall reaction is the same as the rate law that would result if the reaction occurred as an elementary step, then the reaction "
